# Raw downloads: 73 MB, and regenerable byte-for-byte by scripts/fetch_data.py.
# The deterministic curated samples in data/curated/ ARE committed (10 MB), with a
# SHA-256 for each in data/MANIFEST.json.
data/raw/

# Trained artifacts ARE committed -- both the JSON payloads (3.9 MB) and the
# pickled pipelines (16 MB). That is a deliberate choice: it means a fresh clone
# can serve the console and run live inference immediately, instead of requiring
# an hour of training before anything renders. They are regenerable with
# `python scripts/train_all.py`, and every one carries the timestamp, seed,
# Python version and platform of the run that produced it. The commit is stamped
# too when training runs inside a git checkout; the committed artifacts were
# trained before this repository was initialised, so theirs reads `n/a`.
#
# scikit-learn pickles are version-sensitive, so requirements.txt is pinned; if a
# pickle fails to load, retraining is the supported fix.

